「呼…」%K%P
Having gone into the convenience store as a temporary\nrespite from the cold, exiting the store into the chilly\nevening winter's breeze made me want to step right back\ninside again.%K%P
我为了躲避严寒而进入便利店，刚一出来，\n初冬一季不变的寒气又在身边扩散开了。%K%P
However, I was the kind of timid person that started\nfeeling awkward after ten or so minutes of dawdling around\nin a public establishment, so going in after I had already\nleft was a bit too much for me.%K%P
这让我不禁想要再回到刚才那个温暖之处了，\n但是对于我这个在里面待了１０分就感到难受的胆小鬼来说，\n再次进店恐怕会更加吃不消。%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dIt's already past eleven, huh.\d%K%P
「已经过了１１点了么」%K%P
I glanced at the watch on my left wrist, slightly raising\nthe plastic bag currently filled with pizza-flavored\npotato chips. The minute and hour hands were forming a\nsmall triangle.%K%P
我卷起提着装有比萨的便利店袋子的左手袖子，看了看手表，\n只见长针和短针刚好是左右对称着分布的。%K%P
I guess it was about time I went back...%K%P
差不多该回去了吧…%K%P
Still, it was surprisingly noisy here at this late hour. I\nthought it was a calm neighborhood like East Hagimori.%K%P
不过，都这个点了还是很热闹啊。\n虽然东荻守也是与这差不多的住宅街就是了。%K%P
%LCPasserby 1 (male)
%LC路人１（男）
